    "message": "fix(view): say when -p was not honoured, and show the URL in status\n\nFollow-up to #358, which stopped the already-running branch printing an\nunreachable URL built from the port just requested. It reports the real\nport now, but says nothing about the request, so `ix view -p 19124`\nagainst a server on 19123 prints a correct URL for a port nobody asked\nfor and never mentions the flag was ignored — you find out by noticing\nthe number changed.\n\nWarns on the mismatch instead, keyed on whether -p was typed rather than\nwhether it differs from 8080: comparing against the default would stay\nsilent for someone who explicitly passed `-p 8080` to a server running\nelsewhere, which is the case they typed the flag to find out about, and\nwould nag anyone who typed nothing at all.\n\n`ix view status` also prints the URL now. The port is recorded as of\n#358, so status can finally answer the question people run it to ask. It\nstays silent rather than guessing for an instance old enough to have\nneither a port file nor a server script to recover one from.\n\nThe decision is pulled out as a pure function — inline in the command\naction it could only be exercised by launching a detached server.",
